    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Given that $\\frac{3}{8}=0.375$, complete each statement with $=$ or $\\approx$.\n(a) $\\frac{3}{8} \\; \\square \\; 0.375$\n(b) $\\frac{3}{8} \\; \\square \\; 0.38$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $0.375$ is the exact value, so $\\frac{3}{8}=0.375$.\n(b) $0.38$ is rounded to two decimal places, so $\\frac{3}{8}\\approx0.38$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Round $4.7269$ to three decimal places and write your answer using approximation notation.",
        "solution_text": "The third decimal digit is $6$. The next digit is $9$, so round up to $4.727$.\n$4.7269\\approx4.727$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For each situation, say whether an exact value or an approximation is appropriate.\n(a) A bill comes to exactly $\\$23.47$.\n(b) A length is measured as $2.6831$ m and is to be recorded to two decimal places.",
        "solution_text": "(a) The bill is stated to be exact, so record $\\$23.47$ as an exact amount.\n(b) A measurement is approximate. Rounded to two decimal places, the length is approximately $2.68$ m."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Round $3.998$ to two decimal places and write your answer using approximation notation.",
        "solution_text": "Cut after the hundredths digit. The critical digit is $8$, so round up. Carry from the hundredths through the tenths into the whole-number part.\n$3.998\\approx4.00$"
      }
    ],
